  b6195ad2f55cd26a t("Trigger: the table itself measures whether its columns fit its frame (container width vs table width, re-measured on resize and on new rows). Fits → table with sticky header. Does not fit → each row becomes a block: the name cell (row header) on top, then every other column as label : value, labels taken from the column headers. A fixed breakpoint is not used: it would still overflow a wide table on a 1100 window or stack a 3-column table that fits. Sorting and row open stay the same.",Inter,12,r,align(l),lh(1.5)) p(32,484) s(1200,hug:54) f[(115ec4cd56f36f6e,#9A9A9F)] "Text 264"
